			<string key="arguments" value="{&quot;summary&quot;: &quot;Customer Amelia Davis (user ID: amelia_davis_8890) wants to cancel three remaining reservations due to change of plans, even if non-refundable:\n\n1. MSJ4OA - DFW \u2192 SFO, economy, May 22, 2024, 3 passengers, has travel insurance (but reason is change of plans, not health/weather)\n2. XAZ3C0 - ATL \u2192 CLT, basic economy, May 27, 2024, 2 passengers, no insurance\n3. UDMOP1 - SFO round trip via PHX/PHL, basic economy, May 28-29, 2024, 1 passenger, no insurance\n\nThese do not meet standard cancellation criteria (not business class, not booked within 24 hours, and the travel insurance doesn't cover \&quot;change of plans\&quot;). Customer understands she may forfeit the money but wants to cancel anyway to free up seats for other travelers. Agent already cancelled two eligible business class reservations (8C8K4E and LU15PA) with refunds.&quot;}" />
